  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The reference open-source platform for running medical imaging AI challenges and deploying clinical validation algorithms — 100k+ users, 390+ challenges hosted, including CAMELYON, PANDA, and PI-CAI. Apache 2.0, actively maintained by DIAG Nijmegen (v2025.11, November 2025), self-hostable via Docker Compose. Uniquely covers the full lifecycle from data archiving and expert annotation through challenge benchmarking to algorithm deployment. No comparable open-source alternative at this scope. Essential infrastructure for any team organising medical imaging benchmarks or validating AI algorithms.",
